Likutay Halachos &mdash; Yoreh Day&lsquo;ah

Hilchos Gairim (Laws of Converts)

Halachah 3

Inyan Giyur, Mishpat, v&rsquo;Binyan Bais ha-Mikdash &mdash; The Matter of Conversion, Judgment, and the Building of the Holy Temple

According to the Torah-teaching that begins: &ldquo;One who

continually strives to draw human beings to the service of the Blessed One&rdquo;

((Siman 59 in Likutay Moharan, Part One)), see there.

And it is explained there that one who strives to draw people close to the Blessed One must

guard himself so that the k&rsquo;lipos [husks] and the evil

of those people not take hold of him. For this person who strives to draw close and to

&ldquo;make souls,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; he is building the aspect of the

Haichal ha-Kodesh [the Holy Temple]. And the remedy against this

&mdash; to be saved from the evil of those people he is bringing close, so that it not take

hold of his heart &mdash; is that he summon the angels of his heart, which is the aspect

of the hislahavus ha-lev [the blazing of the heart]. This is

accomplished through the aspect of mishpat [judgment] &mdash;

that a person judges himself &mdash; which is the aspect of fire, in the aspect of

&ldquo;by fire of God shall judgment be rendered&rdquo;
